 ## Overview
-Universal Beta Splatting (UBS) is a unified framework for explicit radiance field rendering that generalizes 3D Gaussian Splatting to N-dimensional anisotropic Beta kernels [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of modeling complex light transport, view-dependent appearance, and scene dynamics simultaneously without requiring auxiliary color encodings (such as spherical harmonics) or separate networks [S1, unofficial]. Unlike its siblings, UBS natively incorporates view and temporal dimensions into the kernel's query space, allowing the primitive's mean and covariance to adapt to these conditions via Beta-modulated conditional slicing [S1, unofficial]. This approach achieves significant parameter efficiency (e.g., 41% reduction over 3DGS for static scenes) while maintaining backward compatibility with Gaussian splatting as a special case [S1, unofficial].
